      type: "MSQ",
      text: `<p></p> <p>Suppose that you live in a one-dimensional world with your house at position 0, as shown here:</p> <p style="text-align:center"><img alt="" height="125" src="js/questions/fst-mock-test-6/20.png" width="720"/></p> <p>One day, you decide to go for a walk by taking steps of size \\(\\pm 1\\) forward and backward. You begin at your house and, after completing your walk, end up back at your house. </p> <p>Consider the alphabet \\(\\Sigma=\\{\\mathbf{L}, \\mathbf{R}\\}\\). A string in \\(\\Sigma^*\\) describes a possible walk where at each step you either move a step left \\((\\mathrm{L})\\) or a step right \\((\\mathrm{R})\\). For example, the string \\(\\text{"LRRRLL"}\\) means that you take a step left, then three steps right, then two steps left. </p> <p>Let \\(\\text{L}=\\left\\{w \\in \\Sigma^* \\mid w\\right.\\) describes a series of steps in which you arrive at the same place at which you started \\(\\}\\).<br/> Which of the following CFGs(Context-Free Grammars) does not generate language \\(\\text{L}?\\) </p> <p></p>`,
