      text: `<p></p> <p>Let \\( S = \\{a,b\\} \\) be an alphabet, with total order \\( a &lt; b \\). Let \\( \\Sigma = S^* \\) be the set of all strings over \\( S \\); for \\( w = s_1 s_2 \\ldots s_n \\in \\Sigma \\) we write \\( \\ell(w) = n \\), and for \\( 1 \\le r \\le n = \\ell(w) \\) we write \\( w_r = s_1 s_2 \\ldots s_r \\). Denote by \\( \\varepsilon \\) the unique word of \\( \\Sigma \\) such that \\( \\ell(\\varepsilon) = 0 \\), the <em>null string</em>. Conventionally \\( w_0 = \\varepsilon \\) for all words \\( w \\in \\Sigma \\). </p> <p>Define relation \\( \\prec \\) on \\( \\Sigma \\) as follows: </p> <p>Let \\( v, w \\in \\Sigma \\), and \\( n = \\min\\{\\ell(v), \\ell(w)\\} \\). Let \\( r = \\max\\{\\, i \\mid v_i = w_i \\,\\} \\le n \\) . </p> <p>Then \\( v \\prec w \\) if: </p> <p>either (i) \\( \\ell(v) = r \\); </p> <p>or (ii) \\( v_{r+1} = v_r a,\\; w_{r+1} = w_r b \\), where \\( v_r = w_r \\). </p> <p>Which of following conditions are satisfied by \\( (\\Sigma, \\prec) \\)? (Select all that apply) </p> <p></p>`,
